tle\":\"Two Sum with Target Lookup\",\"prompt\":\"Given an array of integers and a target integer, find the indices of two different elements whose sum equals the target. Print the two indices in increasing order. Exactly one valid pair exists.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"constraints\":\"2 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^9 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^9\\nExactly one valid answer exists.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Traverse the array once and use a HashMap to store previously visited numbers and their indices. For each number, check whether target - nums[i] already exists.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.716Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.716Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"input\":\"4\\n2 7 11 15\\n9\",\"expected_output\":\"0 1\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.741Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.741Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":1,\"input\":\"5\\n3 3 8 2 10\\n6\",\"expected_output\":\"0 1\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.747Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.747Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Can you store already visited numbers and look for target - current number?\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.753Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.753Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":1,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why a nested-loop solution becomes O(N^2).\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Valid Anagram\",\"prompt\":\"Given two strings, determine whether they are anagrams of each other. Two strings are anagrams if they contain exactly the same characters with the same frequencies.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":2,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length, t.length \\u003c= 10^5\\nStrings contain lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Count the frequency of every character in the first string and compare it with the frequency of characters in the second string using a HashMap or frequency array.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"anagram\\nnagaram\",\"expected_output\":\"true\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"rat\\ncar\",\"expected_output\":\"false\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Think about how to count the frequency of each character.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask whether sorting both strings is necessary and what its complexity would be.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.848Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.848Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.811Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.811Z\"},{\"id\":3,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"First Non-Repeating Character\",\"prompt\":\"Given a string, find the index of the first character that appears exactly once. If no such character exists, print -1.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":3,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length \\u003c= 10^5\\ns consists of lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Build a frequency map for all characters, then make a second pass through the string and return the index of the first character whose frequency is one.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.9Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.9Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":5,\"question_id\":3,\"input\":\"leetcode\",\"expected_output\":\"0\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.915Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.915Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"question_id\":3,\"input\":\"aabbcc\",\"expected_output\":\"-1\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.917Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.917Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":5,\"question_id\":3,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"First count how many times every character occurs.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.926Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.926Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"question_id\":3,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why two passes still result in O(N) time.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.932Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.932Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.891Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.891Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Group Anagrams\",\"prompt\":\"Given N strings, group strings that are anagrams of each other. Print each group on a separate line. Words within each group should remain in their original input order.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":4,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^4\\n1 \\u003c= word.length \\u003c= 100\\nWords contain lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Create a character-frequency signature for each word and use that signature as a HashMap key. Words with the same signature belong to the same group.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N * L), Space: O(N * L)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.983Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.983Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":7,\"question_id\":4,\"input\":\"6\\neat tea tan ate nat bat\",\"expected_output\":\"eat tea ate\\ntan nat\\nbat\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.988Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.988Z\"},{\"id\":8,\"question_id\":4,\"input\":\"5\\nabc cba bac xyz zyx\",\"expected_output\":\"abc cba bac\\nxyz zyx\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.994Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.994Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":7,\"question_id\":4,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Anagrams have the same character frequencies.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40Z\"},{\"id\":8,\"question_id\":4,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask the candidate to compare a sorted-string key with a frequency-based key.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.002Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.002Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.974Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.974Z\"},{\"id\":5,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters\",\"prompt\":\"Given a string, find the length of the longest substring that contains no repeated characters.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":5,\"question_id\":5,\"constraints\":\"0 \\u003c= s.length \\u003c= 10^5\\ns consists of printable ASCII characters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use a sliding window with two pointers and a HashMap storing the most recent index of each character.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.058Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.058Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":9,\"question_id\":5,\"input\":\"abcabcbb\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.069Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.069Z\"},{\"id\":10,\"question_id\":5,\"input\":\"pwwkew\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.073Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.073Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":9,\"question_id\":5,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Maintain a window that contains only unique characters.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.083Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.083Z\"},{\"id\":10,\"question_id\":5,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the left pointer should move when a duplicate character is found.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.085Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.085Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.051Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.051Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Majority Element\",\"prompt\":\"Given an array of integers, find the element that appears more than N/2 times. A majority element is guaranteed to exist.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":6,\"question_id\":6,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^9 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^9\\nA majority element always exists.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm to maintain a candidate and a count while traversing the array.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(1)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.131Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.131Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":11,\"question_id\":6,\"input\":\"7\\n2 2 1 1 1 2 2\",\"expected_output\":\"2\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.145Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.145Z\"},{\"id\":12,\"question_id\":6,\"input\":\"5\\n3 3 4 3 3\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.148Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.148Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":11,\"question_id\":6,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"You can first think about counting frequencies with a HashMap.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.155Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.155Z\"},{\"id\":12,\"question_id\":6,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask whether the candidate can reduce the auxiliary space to O(1).\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.162Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.162Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.12Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.12Z\"},{\"id\":7,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Longest Consecutive Sequence\",\"prompt\":\"Given an unsorted array of integers, find the length of the longest sequence of consecutive integers. The elements do not need to appear next to each other in the input array.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":7,\"question_id\":7,\"constraints\":\"0 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^9 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^9\\nDuplicate values may exist.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Insert all values into a HashSet. Start counting a sequence only when the current value has no predecessor, then repeatedly check for the next consecutive value.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N) average, Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.2Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.2Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":13,\"question_id\":7,\"input\":\"6\\n100 4 200 1 3 2\",\"expected_output\":\"4\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.206Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.206Z\"},{\"id\":14,\"question_id\":7,\"input\":\"8\\n0 3 7 2 5 8 4 6\",\"expected_output\":\"7\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.212Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.212Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":13,\"question_id\":7,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Try putting all numbers into a HashSet.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.217Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.217Z\"},{\"id\":14,\"question_id\":7,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why sorting is not required and how duplicates are handled.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.217Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.217Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.194Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.194Z\"},{\"id\":8,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Product of Array Except Self\",\"prompt\":\"Given an integer array, return an array where each position contains the product of every element except the element at that position. Division is not allowed.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":8,\"question_id\":8,\"constraints\":\"2 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-30 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 30\\nThe result fits within a 32-bit signed integer.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Calculate prefix products from left to right and suffix products from right to left without using division.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(1) auxiliary excluding the output array\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.261Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.261Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":15,\"question_id\":8,\"input\":\"4\\n1 2 3 4\",\"expected_output\":\"24 12 8 6\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.267Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.267Z\"},{\"id\":16,\"question_id\":8,\"input\":\"4\\n-1 1 0 -3\",\"expected_output\":\"0 0 3 0\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.268Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.268Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":15,\"question_id\":8,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"For every position, think about the product of elements on its left and right.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.273Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.273Z\"},{\"id\":16,\"question_id\":8,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why division is problematic when the array contains zero.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.278Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.278Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.252Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.252Z\"},{\"id\":9,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Subarray Sum Equals K\",\"prompt\":\"Given an integer array and an integer K, count the number of contiguous subarrays whose sum equals K.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":9,\"question_id\":9,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^4 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^4\\n-10^9 \\u003c= K \\u003c= 10^9\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Maintain a running prefix sum and use a HashMap to store the frequency of previous prefix sums. For the current sum S, look for S - K.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":17,\"question_id\":9,\"input\":\"3\\n1 1 1\\n2\",\"expected_output\":\"2\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.322Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.322Z\"},{\"id\":18,\"question_id\":9,\"input\":\"3\\n1 -1 0\\n0\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.328Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.328Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":17,\"question_id\":9,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Think about prefix sums and what previous sum would be needed to produce K.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.334Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.334Z\"},{\"id\":18,\"question_id\":9,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why a normal sliding-window approach does not work when negative numbers are present.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.335Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.335Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.307Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.307Z\"},{\"id\":10,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Valid Parentheses\",\"prompt\":\"Given a string containing only (), {}, and [], determine whether the brackets are valid. Every opening bracket must have the correct closing bracket, and brackets must close in the correct order.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":10,\"question_id\":10,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length \\u003c= 10^5\\ns contains only (, ), {, }, [, ].\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use a stack to store opening brackets and verify that every closing bracket matches the most recently opened bracket.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.382Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.382Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":19,\"question_id\":10,\"input\":\"{[()]}\",\"expected_output\":\"true\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.388Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.388Z\"},{\"id\":20,\"question_id\":10,\"input\":\"([)]\",\"expected_output\":\"false\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.395Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.395Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":19,\"question_id\":10,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"The most recently opened bracket must be closed first.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.401Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.401Z\"},{\"id\":20,\"question_id\":10,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why a stack is suitable for this problem and what happens when a closing bracket appears with an empty stack.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.402Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.402Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.371Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.371Z\"}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:17.505'),(347,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/1/levels','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,5,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":1,\"track_id\":1,\"level_number\":1,\"name\":\"Arrays, Strings \\u0026 HashMaps\",\"description\":\"Fundamental data structures and two-pointer techniques\",\"mode\":\"coding\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:25.437Z\",\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":2,\"track_id\":1,\"level_number\":2,\"name\":\"Trees, Graphs \\u0026 Recursion\",\"description\":\"Tree traversals, BFS/DFS algorithms, and topological sorting\",\"mode\":\"coding\",\"duration_minutes\":50,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:35.989Z\",\"questions_count\":0},{\"id\":3,\"track_id\":1,\"level_number\":3,\"name\":\"Dynamic Programming \\u0026 Optimization\",\"description\":\"State transitions, memoization, and hard algorithmic challenges\",\"mode\":\"coding\",\"duration_minutes\":60,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:42.721Z\",\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:19.504'),(348,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/1','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Technical\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Core problem solving, arrays, trees, dynamic programming, and algorithmic complexity.\",\"icon\":\"Code\",\"id\":1,\"levels_count\":3,\"questions_count\":10,\"slug\":\"dsa\",\"title\":\"Data Structures \\u0026 Algorithms\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:19.542'),(349,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,14,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":1,\"title\":\"Data Structures \\u0026 Algorithms\",\"slug\":\"dsa\",\"category\":\"Technical\",\"icon\":\"Code\",\"description\":\"Core problem solving, arrays, trees, dynamic programming, and algorithmic complexity.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":3,\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":2,\"title\":\"System Design \\u0026 Architecture\",\"slug\":\"system-design\",\"category\":\"Architecture\",\"icon\":\"Layers\",\"description\":\"Scalable distributed systems, load balancers, caching, microservices, and whiteboard diagrams.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":3,\"title\":\"Database Engineering \\u0026 SQL\",\"slug\":\"database-engineering\",\"category\":\"Databases\",\"icon\":\"Database\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground, schema design, indexes, transactions, and query optimization.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":4,\"title\":\"Frontend \\u0026 Web Development\",\"slug\":\"frontend-dev\",\"category\":\"Web\",\"icon\":\"Layout\",\"description\":\"React, JavaScript/TypeScript, UI components, state management, and web performance.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":5,\"title\":\"Backend \\u0026 API Systems\",\"slug\":\"backend-systems\",\"category\":\"Backend\",\"icon\":\"Server\",\"description\":\"RESTful APIs, authentication, microservice orchestration, concurrency, and security.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":6,\"title\":\"Computer Science Fundamentals\",\"slug\":\"cs-fundamentals\",\"category\":\"Core CS\",\"icon\":\"CheckSquare\",\"description\":\"Speed assessment on Operating Systems, Computer Networks, DBMS, and OOPs concepts.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":0},{\"id\":7,\"title\":\"Behavioral \\u0026 Leadership\",\"slug\":\"behavioral-leadership\",\"category\":\"HR \\u0026 Soft Skills\",\"icon\":\"Users\",\"description\":\"STAR format behavioral inquiries, culture fit, conflict resolution, and leadership principles.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:20.527'),(350,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/2/levels','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":4,\"track_id\":2,\"level_number\":1,\"name\":\"High-Level System Design\",\"description\":\"Designing scalable URL shorteners, rate limiters, and cache layers\",\"mode\":\"whiteboard\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":5,\"track_id\":2,\"level_number\":2,\"name\":\"Large-Scale Distributed Systems\",\"description\":\"Designing YouTube, Uber, or messaging systems with partitioning and CAP theorem\",\"mode\":\"whiteboard\",\"duration_minutes\":60,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:21.467'),(351,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/2','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,6,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Architecture\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Scalable distributed systems, load balancers, caching, microservices, and whiteboard diagrams.\",\"icon\":\"Layers\",\"id\":2,\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":10,\"slug\":\"system-design\",\"title\":\"System Design \\u0026 Architecture\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:21.515'),(352,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/levels/4','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,5,'','{\"data\":{\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"description\":\"Designing scalable URL shorteners, rate limiters, and cache layers\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"id\":4,\"level_number\":1,\"mode\":\"whiteboard\",\"name\":\"High-Level System Design\",\"question_count\":1,\"questions_count\":10,\"track_id\":2,\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:23.193'),(353,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/2','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,6,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Architecture\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Scalable distributed systems, load balancers, caching, microservices, and whiteboard diagrams.\",\"icon\":\"Layers\",\"id\":2,\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":10,\"slug\":\"system-design\",\"title\":\"System Design \\u0026 Architecture\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:23.194'),(354,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/levels/4/questions','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,13,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":11,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a URL Shortener\",\"prompt\":\"Design a scalable URL shortening service that converts long URLs into short aliases and redirects users to the original URL.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":11,\"question_id\":11,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"500M new URLs per month and 50B redirects per month. Read/write ratio is approximately 100:1. Redirect latency should be below 10ms with 99.99% availability.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.376Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.376Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":21,\"question_id\":11,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Consider Base62 encoding with a distributed ID generator for creating short URLs.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.382Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.382Z\"},{\"id\":22,\"question_id\":11,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use Redis caching for frequently accessed short URLs.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.383Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.383Z\"},{\"id\":23,\"question_id\":11,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss 301 versus 302 redirects and their impact on caching, server load, and analytics.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.384Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.384Z\"},{\"id\":24,\"question_id\":11,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the database should be sharded as the number of URLs grows.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.385Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.385Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.367Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.367Z\"},{\"id\":12,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Real-Time Chat System\",\"prompt\":\"Design a real-time messaging platform that supports one-to-one and group conversations with message delivery, online presence, and message history.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":12,\"question_id\":12,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"10M daily active users with up to 1M concurrent connections. Messages should normally be delivered within 500ms. The system must support message persistence and temporary offline users.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.432Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.432Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":25,\"question_id\":12,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Consider WebSockets for persistent real-time connections.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.436Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.436Z\"},{\"id\":26,\"question_id\":12,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use a message queue such as Kafka to decouple message ingestion from delivery.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.445Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.445Z\"},{\"id\":27,\"question_id\":12,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss at-most-once, at-least-once, and effectively-once message delivery.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.446Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.446Z\"},{\"id\":28,\"question_id\":12,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how messages are delivered when the recipient is temporarily offline.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.447Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.447Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.431Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.431Z\"},{\"id\":13,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Video Streaming Platform\",\"prompt\":\"Design a video streaming service where users can upload videos, browse available content, and stream videos with minimal buffering.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":13,\"question_id\":13,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"5M daily active users and 500K video uploads per day. Popular videos may receive millions of views. The system should support adaptive streaming and high availability.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.48Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.48Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":29,\"question_id\":13,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use object storage for video files and a CDN for global delivery.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.483Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.483Z\"},{\"id\":30,\"question_id\":13,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Transcode uploaded videos into multiple resolutions and bitrates.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.483Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.483Z\"},{\"id\":31,\"question_id\":13,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss storage cost versus video quality and the number of generated resolutions.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.484Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.484Z\"},{\"id\":32,\"question_id\":13,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the system handles a sudden traffic spike for a viral video.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.486Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.486Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.477Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.477Z\"},{\"id\":14,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design an Online Food Delivery System\",\"prompt\":\"Design an online food delivery platform where customers can discover restaurants, place orders, make payments, and track delivery status in real time.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":14,\"question_id\":14,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"2M daily users, 100K concurrent users during peak hours, and 200K orders per day. Order creation and payment operations require strong consistency while restaurant discovery can tolerate eventual consistency.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.532Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.532Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":33,\"question_id\":14,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Separate order management, payment, restaurant, and delivery services.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.545Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.545Z\"},{\"id\":34,\"question_id\":14,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use asynchronous events for order status updates and delivery tracking.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.549Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.549Z\"},{\"id\":35,\"question_id\":14,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss strong consistency for orders and payments versus eventual consistency for restaurant availability and tracking.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.55Z\"},{\"id\":36,\"question_id\":14,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how duplicate payment requests and duplicate orders are prevented.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.553Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.553Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.525Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.525Z\"},{\"id\":15,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Ride-Sharing System\",\"prompt\":\"Design a ride-sharing platform that allows passengers to request rides, matches them with nearby drivers, and tracks rides in real time.\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":15,\"question_id\":15,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"5M daily active users and 500K concurrent drivers. Location updates can arrive every few seconds. Ride matching should normally complete within 2 seconds.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.635Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.635Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":37,\"question_id\":15,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use geospatial indexing to find nearby available drivers efficiently.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.648Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.648Z\"},{\"id\":38,\"question_id\":15,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use WebSockets or similar persistent connections for real-time location updates.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.65Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.65Z\"},{\"id\":39,\"question_id\":15,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss location-update frequency versus network, CPU, and storage costs.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.653Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.653Z\"},{\"id\":40,\"question_id\":15,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the system prevents two passengers from being assigned the same driver.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.666Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.666Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.618Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.618Z\"},{\"id\":16,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Distributed Rate Limiter\",\"prompt\":\"Design a distributed rate-limiting service that protects APIs from excessive requests while supporting multiple application servers.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":16,\"question_id\":16,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"The platform receives 1M requests per second across multiple regions. Different APIs may have different limits per user, IP address, or API key. Rate-limit decisions should normally complete within 5ms.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.732Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.732Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":41,\"question_id\":16,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Consider token bucket or sliding-window algorithms.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.749Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.749Z\"},{\"id\":42,\"question_id\":16,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use Redis or another distributed store for shared counters.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.754Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.754Z\"},{\"id\":43,\"question_id\":16,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss exact global limits versus local limits with lower latency.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.762Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.762Z\"},{\"id\":44,\"question_id\":16,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask what happens when the Redis cluster becomes temporarily unavailable.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.765Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.765Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.717Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.717Z\"},{\"id\":17,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Notification System\",\"prompt\":\"Design a notification platform capable of sending push notifications, emails, and SMS messages based on events generated by different applications.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":17,\"question_id\":17,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"100M notifications per day with large traffic bursts. Notifications should be processed asynchronously, retried when providers fail, and should not block the application\'s main request path.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.814Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.814Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":45,\"question_id\":17,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use a message queue between event producers and notification workers.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.825Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.825Z\"},{\"id\":46,\"question_id\":17,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use retry queues and dead-letter queues for failed notifications.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.83Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.83Z\"},{\"id\":47,\"question_id\":17,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss delivery guarantees versus duplicate notifications.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.831Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.831Z\"},{\"id\":48,\"question_id\":17,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how notification preferences and user-specific rate limits should be enforced.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.832Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.832Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.811Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.811Z\"},{\"id\":18,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Distributed File Storage System\",\"prompt\":\"Design a cloud file-storage service where users can upload, download, organize, and share files across multiple devices.\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":18,\"question_id\":18,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"50M users with 10PB of stored data. Individual files can range from a few KB to several GB. The system must provide durable storage and efficient downloads.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.882Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.882Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":49,\"question_id\":18,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use object storage with metadata stored separately in a database.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.897Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.897Z\"},{\"id\":50,\"question_id\":18,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Consider multipart uploads for large files and CDN caching for frequently downloaded files.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.899Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.899Z\"},{\"id\":51,\"question_id\":18,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss replication level, durability, storage cost, and access latency.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.9Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.9Z\"},{\"id\":52,\"question_id\":18,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how concurrent updates to the same file should be handled.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.902Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.902Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.87Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.87Z\"},{\"id\":19,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design an E-Commerce Platform\",\"prompt\":\"Design a scalable e-commerce platform where users can browse products, search inventory, add items to carts, place orders, and complete payments.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":19,\"question_id\":19,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"10M daily users with 100K concurrent users during major sales. Product browsing is read-heavy, while inventory and order operations require strong consistency.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.946Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.946Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":53,\"question_id\":19,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use caching and read replicas for high-volume product browsing.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.948Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.948Z\"},{\"id\":54,\"question_id\":19,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use atomic inventory operations to prevent overselling during high-demand sales.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.949Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.949Z\"},{\"id\":55,\"question_id\":19,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss database consistency versus availability for inventory and product information.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.95Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.95Z\"},{\"id\":56,\"question_id\":19,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the system handles thousands of users attempting to purchase the last item simultaneously.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.95Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.95Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.935Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.935Z\"},{\"id\":20,\"level_id\":4,\"title\":\"Design a Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor\",\"prompt\":\"Architect a real-time collaborative text editor that allows multiple users to edit the same document simultaneously while resolving conflicts and maintaining document history.\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"type\":\"whiteboard\",\"detail\":{\"id\":20,\"question_id\":20,\"constraints\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"100 active collaborators per document with typing latency below 50ms. The system must support document revisions, concurrent edits, and users reconnecting after temporary network failures.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.998Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.998Z\"},\"hints\":[{\"id\":57,\"question_id\":20,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Consider Operational Transformation or Conflict-free Replicated Data Types for concurrent editing.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.009Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.009Z\"},{\"id\":58,\"question_id\":20,\"type\":\"talking_point\",\"content\":\"Use WebSockets for real-time updates and a persistent store for document snapshots and history.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.014Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.014Z\"},{\"id\":59,\"question_id\":20,\"type\":\"tradeoff\",\"content\":\"Discuss centralized operation ordering with OT versus client-side convergence with CRDTs.\",\"order_index\":3,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.016Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.016Z\"},{\"id\":60,\"question_id\":20,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how document snapshotting prevents replaying a very large number of historical operations.\",\"order_index\":4,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.017Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:24.017Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.988Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:23.988Z\"}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:23.193'),(355,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/2','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Architecture\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Scalable distributed systems, load balancers, caching, microservices, and whiteboard diagrams.\",\"icon\":\"Layers\",\"id\":2,\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":10,\"slug\":\"system-design\",\"title\":\"System Design \\u0026 Architecture\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:25.849'),(356,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/2/levels','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":4,\"track_id\":2,\"level_number\":1,\"name\":\"High-Level System Design\",\"description\":\"Designing scalable URL shorteners, rate limiters, and cache layers\",\"mode\":\"whiteboard\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":5,\"track_id\":2,\"level_number\":2,\"name\":\"Large-Scale Distributed Systems\",\"description\":\"Designing YouTube, Uber, or messaging systems with partitioning and CAP theorem\",\"mode\":\"whiteboard\",\"duration_minutes\":60,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:25.891'),(357,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,10,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":1,\"title\":\"Data Structures \\u0026 Algorithms\",\"slug\":\"dsa\",\"category\":\"Technical\",\"icon\":\"Code\",\"description\":\"Core problem solving, arrays, trees, dynamic programming, and algorithmic complexity.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":3,\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":2,\"title\":\"System Design \\u0026 Architecture\",\"slug\":\"system-design\",\"category\":\"Architecture\",\"icon\":\"Layers\",\"description\":\"Scalable distributed systems, load balancers, caching, microservices, and whiteboard diagrams.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":10},{\"id\":3,\"title\":\"Database Engineering \\u0026 SQL\",\"slug\":\"database-engineering\",\"category\":\"Databases\",\"icon\":\"Database\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground, schema design, indexes, transactions, and query optimization.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":4,\"title\":\"Frontend \\u0026 Web Development\",\"slug\":\"frontend-dev\",\"category\":\"Web\",\"icon\":\"Layout\",\"description\":\"React, JavaScript/TypeScript, UI components, state management, and web performance.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":5,\"title\":\"Backend \\u0026 API Systems\",\"slug\":\"backend-systems\",\"category\":\"Backend\",\"icon\":\"Server\",\"description\":\"RESTful APIs, authentication, microservice orchestration, concurrency, and security.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":6,\"title\":\"Computer Science Fundamentals\",\"slug\":\"cs-fundamentals\",\"category\":\"Core CS\",\"icon\":\"CheckSquare\",\"description\":\"Speed assessment on Operating Systems, Computer Networks, DBMS, and OOPs concepts.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":0},{\"id\":7,\"title\":\"Behavioral \\u0026 Leadership\",\"slug\":\"behavioral-leadership\",\"category\":\"HR \\u0026 Soft Skills\",\"icon\":\"Users\",\"description\":\"STAR format behavioral inquiries, culture fit, conflict resolution, and leadership principles.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:27.121'),(358,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/3','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Databases\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground, schema design, indexes, transactions, and query optimization.\",\"icon\":\"Database\",\"id\":3,\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5,\"slug\":\"database-engineering\",\"title\":\"Database Engineering \\u0026 SQL\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:28.282'),(359,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/3/levels','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,4,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":6,\"track_id\":3,\"level_number\":1,\"name\":\"Relational Queries \\u0026 Complex Joins\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground: aggregations, subqueries, and window functions\",\"mode\":\"database\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:49.616Z\",\"questions_count\":5},{\"id\":7,\"track_id\":3,\"level_number\":2,\"name\":\"Schema Design \\u0026 Query Optimization\",\"description\":\"Indexing strategies, query execution plans, and transaction isolation\",\"mode\":\"database\",\"duration_minutes\":50,\"question_count\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:56.111Z\",\"questions_count\":0}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:28.282'),(360,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/3','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,2,'','{\"data\":{\"category\":\"Databases\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground, schema design, indexes, transactions, and query optimization.\",\"icon\":\"Database\",\"id\":3,\"levels_count\":2,\"questions_count\":5,\"slug\":\"database-engineering\",\"title\":\"Database Engineering \\u0026 SQL\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:43:11Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:29.705'),(361,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/levels/6','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,2,'','{\"data\":{\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:44:11Z\",\"description\":\"Interactive SQL playground: aggregations, subqueries, and window functions\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"id\":6,\"level_number\":1,\"mode\":\"database\",\"name\":\"Relational Queries \\u0026 Complex Joins\",\"question_count\":1,\"questions_count\":5,\"track_id\":3,\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:55:49.616Z\"},\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:29.750'),(362,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/levels/6/questions','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/153.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',200,8,'','{\"data\":[{\"id\":21,\"level_id\":6,\"title\":\"Employee Department Salary Analysis\",\"prompt\":\"Write a SQL query to find the top 3 highest-paid employees in each department, including the employee name, department name, and salary.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"database\",\"detail\":{\"id\":21,\"question_id\":21,\"constraints\":\"Employees without a valid department should not appear. Handle salary ties appropriately.\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use JOIN between employees and departments, then use ROW_NUMBER() or DENSE_RANK() with PARTITION BY department_id to identify the highest-paid employees in each department.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"Tables required: employees, departments. Employees belong to departments and have salary information. Return the top 3 employees per department.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.694Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.694Z\"},\"templates\":[{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":21,\"language\":\"sql\",\"starter_code\":\"CREATE TABLE departments (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE employees (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\\n  department_id INTEGER,\\n  salary DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (department_id) REFERENCES departments(id)\\n);\\n\\nINSERT INTO departments VALUES\\n(1, \'Engineering\'),\\n(2, \'HR\'),\\n(3, \'Finance\');\\n\\nINSERT INTO employees VALUES\\n(101, \'Alice\', 1, 90000),\\n(102, \'Bob\', 1, 110000),\\n(103, \'Charlie\', 1, 105000),\\n(104, \'David\', 2, 70000),\\n(105, \'Eva\', 2, 85000),\\n(106, \'Frank\', 3, 95000);\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.695Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.695Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":61,\"question_id\":21,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Use a window function with PARTITION BY department_id and ORDER BY salary DESC.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.699Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.699Z\"},{\"id\":62,\"question_id\":21,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Evaluate whether the candidate understands the difference between ROW_NUMBER(), RANK(), and DENSE_RANK().\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.703Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.703Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.693Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.693Z\"},{\"id\":22,\"level_id\":6,\"title\":\"Customers Without Recent Orders\",\"prompt\":\"Write a SQL query to find customers who have not placed any completed orders during the last 6 months.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"database\",\"detail\":{\"id\":22,\"question_id\":22,\"constraints\":\"Customers with only pending or refunded orders should also be included.\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use LEFT JOIN with the date and status conditions applied correctly, then identify customers whose matching order is NULL.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"Tables required: customers and orders. A customer can have multiple orders. Only completed orders should be considered.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.73Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.73Z\"},\"templates\":[{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":22,\"language\":\"sql\",\"starter_code\":\"CREATE TABLE customers (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\\n  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE orders (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  customer_id INTEGER,\\n  status VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,\\n  total_amount DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,\\n  created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (customer_id) REFERENCES customers(id)\\n);\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.734Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.734Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":63,\"question_id\":22,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"A LEFT JOIN can preserve customers even when they have no matching recent completed order.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.74Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.74Z\"},{\"id\":64,\"question_id\":22,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Check whether the candidate understands why putting the filtering condition in WHERE instead of ON can change LEFT JOIN behavior.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.741Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.741Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.728Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.728Z\"},{\"id\":23,\"level_id\":6,\"title\":\"Product Sales With Category Ranking\",\"prompt\":\"Write a SQL query to find the highest-selling product in each category based on total quantity sold.\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"type\":\"database\",\"detail\":{\"id\":23,\"question_id\":23,\"constraints\":\"Products with no completed sales should not be considered. Handle multiple products having the same total quantity.\",\"expected_approach\":\"Join products with categories and order_items, filter completed orders, aggregate quantity by product, and use a window function to rank products within each category.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"Tables required: products, categories, order_items, and orders. Only completed orders should contribute to sales calculations.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.774Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.774Z\"},\"templates\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":23,\"language\":\"sql\",\"starter_code\":\"CREATE TABLE categories (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE products (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,\\n  category_id INTEGER,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (category_id) REFERENCES categories(id)\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE orders (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  status VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE order_items (\\n  order_id INTEGER,\\n  product_id INTEGER,\\n  quantity INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (order_id) REFERENCES orders(id),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (product_id) REFERENCES products(id)\\n);\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.776Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.776Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":65,\"question_id\":23,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"First calculate total quantity for each product, then rank products inside each category.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.779Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.779Z\"},{\"id\":66,\"question_id\":23,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Evaluate the candidate\'s ability to combine multiple JOINs, GROUP BY, aggregation, and window functions.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.78Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.78Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.767Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.767Z\"},{\"id\":24,\"level_id\":6,\"title\":\"Department Average Salary Comparison\",\"prompt\":\"Write a SQL query to find employees whose salary is greater than the average salary of their own department.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"database\",\"detail\":{\"id\":24,\"question_id\":24,\"constraints\":\"Return employee name, department name, salary, and department average salary.\",\"expected_approach\":\"Calculate the department-level average salary using a subquery or window function, then compare each employee\'s salary against the corresponding department average.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"Tables required: employees and departments. Each employee belongs to a department and has a salary.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.821Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.821Z\"},\"templates\":[{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":24,\"language\":\"sql\",\"starter_code\":\"CREATE TABLE departments (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE employees (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\\n  department_id INTEGER,\\n  salary DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (department_id) REFERENCES departments(id)\\n);\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.824Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.824Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":67,\"question_id\":24,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"You can calculate the department average using AVG() with PARTITION BY department_id.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.826Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.826Z\"},{\"id\":68,\"question_id\":24,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Check whether the candidate can avoid unnecessary correlated subqueries when a window function can solve the problem.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.828Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.828Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.814Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.814Z\"},{\"id\":25,\"level_id\":6,\"title\":\"Multi-Level Order Customer Analysis\",\"prompt\":\"Write a SQL query to find customers who have purchased at least 3 different products across at least 2 different categories, and calculate their total spending.\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"type\":\"database\",\"detail\":{\"id\":25,\"question_id\":25,\"constraints\":\"A customer must have purchased at least 3 distinct products and products from at least 2 distinct categories.\",\"expected_approach\":\"Join all related tables, filter completed orders, group by customer, calculate COUNT(DISTINCT product_id), COUNT(DISTINCT category_id), and SUM of item quantity multiplied by product price.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"Tables required: customers, orders, order_items, products, and categories. Only completed orders should be included.\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.873Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.873Z\"},\"templates\":[{\"id\":5,\"question_id\":25,\"language\":\"sql\",\"starter_code\":\"CREATE TABLE customers (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE categories (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE products (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,\\n  category_id INTEGER,\\n  price DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (category_id) REFERENCES categories(id)\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE orders (\\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\\n  customer_id INTEGER,\\n  status VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (customer_id) REFERENCES customers(id)\\n);\\n\\nCREATE TABLE order_items (\\n  order_id INTEGER,\\n  product_id INTEGER,\\n  quantity INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n  FOREIGN KEY (order_id) REFERENCES orders(id),\\n  FOREIGN KEY (product_id) REFERENCES products(id)\\n);\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.875Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.875Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":69,\"question_id\":25,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Use COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) and COUNT(DISTINCT category_id) with HAVING.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.877Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.877Z\"},{\"id\":70,\"question_id\":25,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Evaluate whether the candidate understands the difference between WHERE and HAVING when filtering aggregated results.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.88Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.88Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.867Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:59:35.867Z\"}],\"status\":\"success\"}','','2026-09-17 08:04:29.751'),(363,2,'admin@bitsathy.ac.in','System Administrator','admin','GET','/api/v1/admin/interviews/tracks/3','','2a09:bac1:36c0:128::2a7:70','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/53