intain a running prefix sum and use a HashMap to store the frequency of previous prefix sums. For the current sum S, look for S - K.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\"},\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"id\":9,\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"interview_tips\":[\"Ask why a normal sliding-window approach does not work when negative numbers are present.\"],\"level_id\":1,\"mcq_options\":null,\"options\":null,\"payload\":{\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^4 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^4\\n-10^9 \\u003c= K \\u003c= 10^9\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"expected_approach\":\"Maintain a running prefix sum and use a HashMap to store the frequency of previous prefix sums. For the current sum S, look for S - K.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"hints\":[\"Think about prefix sums and what previous sum would be needed to produce K.\"],\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"interview_tips\":[\"Ask why a normal sliding-window approach does not work when negative numbers are present.\"],\"open_test_cases\":[{\"explanation\":\"\",\"input\":\"3\\n1 1 1\\n2\",\"output\":\"2\"}],\"options\":null,\"rubrics\":null,\"scenario\":\"\",\"starter_code\":\"\",\"starter_code_cpp\":\"\",\"starter_code_java\":\"\",\"starter_code_js\":\"\",\"starter_code_py\":\"\",\"talking_points\":null,\"tradeoffs\":null},\"prompt\":\"Given an integer array and an integer K, count the number of contiguous subarrays whose sum equals K.\",\"rubrics\":null,\"talking_points\":null,\"templates\":[],\"test_cases\":[{\"explanation\":\"\",\"input\":\"3\\n1 1 1\\n2\",\"output\":\"2\"}],\"title\":\"Subarray Sum Equals K\",\"tradeoffs\":null,\"type\":\"coding\"},\"current_question_id\":9,\"end_requested_by\":0,\"ended_at\":null,\"id\":1,\"interviewee\":{\"name\":\"Peer Candidate\",\"roll_no\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"department\":\"Student Peer\"},\"interviewee_id\":4,\"interviewer\":{\"name\":\"Jaison David M\",\"email\":\"jaisondavidm.cs25@bitsathy.ac.in\",\"roll_no\":\"7376251CS221\",\"department\":\"CSE\"},\"interviewer_id\":3,\"interviewer_rubrics\":\"\",\"last_executed_at\":null,\"last_execution_json\":\"\",\"last_execution_passed\":0,\"last_execution_total\":0,\"last_execution_type\":\"\",\"last_execution_verdict\":\"\",\"level\":{\"id\":1,\"track_id\":1,\"level_number\":1,\"name\":\"Arrays, Strings \\u0026 HashMaps\",\"description\":\"Fundamental data structures and two-pointer techniques\",\"mode\":\"coding\",\"duration_minutes\":45,\"question_count\":1,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Two Sum with Target Lookup\",\"prompt\":\"Given an array of integers and a target integer, find the indices of two different elements whose sum equals the target. Print the two indices in increasing order. Exactly one valid pair exists.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"constraints\":\"2 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^9 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^9\\nExactly one valid answer exists.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Traverse the array once and use a HashMap to store previously visited numbers and their indices. For each number, check whether target - nums[i] already exists.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.716Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.716Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"input\":\"4\\n2 7 11 15\\n9\",\"expected_output\":\"0 1\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.741Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.741Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":1,\"input\":\"5\\n3 3 8 2 10\\n6\",\"expected_output\":\"0 1\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.747Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.747Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":1,\"question_id\":1,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Can you store already visited numbers and look for target - current number?\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.753Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.753Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":1,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why a nested-loop solution becomes O(N^2).\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Valid Anagram\",\"prompt\":\"Given two strings, determine whether they are anagrams of each other. Two strings are anagrams if they contain exactly the same characters with the same frequencies.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":2,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length, t.length \\u003c= 10^5\\nStrings contain lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Count the frequency of every character in the first string and compare it with the frequency of characters in the second string using a HashMap or frequency array.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"anagram\\nnagaram\",\"expected_output\":\"true\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"rat\\ncar\",\"expected_output\":\"false\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Think about how to count the frequency of each character.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask whether sorting both strings is necessary and what its complexity would be.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.848Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.848Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.811Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.811Z\"},{\"id\":3,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"First Non-Repeating Character\",\"prompt\":\"Given a string, find the index of the first character that appears exactly once. If no such character exists, print -1.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":3,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length \\u003c= 10^5\\ns consists of lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Build a frequency map for all characters, then make a second pass through the string and return the index of the first character whose frequency is one.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.9Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.9Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":5,\"question_id\":3,\"input\":\"leetcode\",\"expected_output\":\"0\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.915Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.915Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"question_id\":3,\"input\":\"aabbcc\",\"expected_output\":\"-1\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.917Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.917Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":5,\"questi