n_id\":1,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why a nested-loop solution becomes O(N^2).\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.761Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.705Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Valid Anagram\",\"prompt\":\"Given two strings, determine whether they are anagrams of each other. Two strings are anagrams if they contain exactly the same characters with the same frequencies.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":2,\"question_id\":2,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= s.length, t.length \\u003c= 10^5\\nStrings contain lowercase English letters.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Count the frequency of every character in the first string and compare it with the frequency of characters in the second string using a HashMap or frequency array.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(K)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.82Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"anagram\\nnagaram\",\"expected_output\":\"true\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.831Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"input\":\"rat\\ncar\",\"expected_output\":\"false\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.833Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":3,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Think about how to count the frequency of each character.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:39.846Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"question_id\":2,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask whether sorting both strings 