 array once and use a HashMap to store previously visited numbers and their indices. For each number, check whether target - nums[i] already exists.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"hints\":[\"Can you store already visited numbers and look for target - current number?\"],\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"interview_tips\":[\"Ask why a nested-loop solution becomes O(N^2).\"],\"open_test_cases\":[{\"explanation\":\"\",\"input\":\"4\\n2 7 11 15\\n9\",\"output\":\"0 1\"}],\"options\":null,\"rubrics\":null,\"scenario\":\"\",\"starter_code\":\"\",\"starter_code_cpp\":\"\",\"starter_code_java\":\"\",\"starter_code_js\":\"\",\"starter_code_py\":\"\",\"talking_points\":null,\"tradeoffs\":null},\"prompt\":\"Given an array of integers and a target integer, find the indices of two different elements whose sum equals the target. Print the two indices in increasing order. Exactly one valid pair exists.\",\"rubrics\":null,\"talking_points\":null,\"templates\":[],\"test_cases\":[{\"explanation\":\"\",\"input\":\"4\\n2 7 11 15\\n9\",\"output\":\"0 1\"}],\"title\":\"Two Sum with Target Lookup\",\"tradeoffs\":null,\"type\":\"coding\"},\"current_question_id\":1,\"end_requested_by\":0,\"ended_at\":null,\"id\":5,\"interviewee\":{\"name\":\"Peer Candidate\",\"roll_no\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"department\":\"Student Peer\"},\"interviewee_id\":4,\"interviewer\":{\"name\":\"Jaison David M\",\"email\":\"jaisondavidm.cs25@bitsathy.ac.in\",\"roll_no\":\"7376251CS221\",\"department\":\"CSE\"},\"interviewer_id\":3,\"interviewer_rubrics\":\"\",\"last_executed_at\":\"2026-09-17T09:31:49.384Z\",\"last_execution_json\":\"{\\\"all_passed\\\":false,\\\"results\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":1,\\\"is_hidden\\\":false,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Sample Case 1\\\",\\\"input\\\":\\\"4\\\\n2 7 11 15\\\\n9\\\",\\\"expected\\\":\\\"0 1\\\",\\\"actual\\\":\\\"Runtime Error:\\\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\\\n  File \\\\\\\"/tmp/mockmate_py_3195247289/solution.py\\\\\\\", line 7, in \\\\u003cmodule\\