indow that contains only unique characters.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.083Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.083Z\"},{\"id\":10,\"question_id\":5,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask how the left pointer should move when a duplicate character is found.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.085Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.085Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.051Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.051Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Majority Element\",\"prompt\":\"Given an array of integers, find the element that appears more than N/2 times. A majority element is guaranteed to exist.\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":6,\"question_id\":6,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^9 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^9\\nA majority element always exists.\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Use the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm to maintain a candidate and a count while traversing the array.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(1)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.131Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.131Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":11,\"question_id\":6,\"input\":\"7\\n2 2 1 1 1 2 2\",\"expected_output\":\"2\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.145Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.145Z\"},{\"id\":12,\"question_id\":6,\"input\":\"5\\n3 3 4 3 3\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.148Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.148Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":11,\"question_id\":6,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"You can first think about counting frequencies with a HashMap.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.155Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07: