\"For every position, think about the product of elements on its left and right.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.273Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.273Z\"},{\"id\":16,\"question_id\":8,\"type\":\"interview_tip\",\"content\":\"Ask why division is problematic when the array contains zero.\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.278Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.278Z\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.252Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.252Z\"},{\"id\":9,\"level_id\":1,\"title\":\"Subarray Sum Equals K\",\"prompt\":\"Given an integer array and an integer K, count the number of contiguous subarrays whose sum equals K.\",\"difficulty\":\"Medium\",\"type\":\"coding\",\"detail\":{\"id\":9,\"question_id\":9,\"constraints\":\"1 \\u003c= N \\u003c= 10^5\\n-10^4 \\u003c= nums[i] \\u003c= 10^4\\n-10^9 \\u003c= K \\u003c= 10^9\\nTime Limit: 2.0s\\nMemory Limit: 256MB\",\"expected_approach\":\"Maintain a running prefix sum and use a HashMap to store the frequency of previous prefix sums. For the current sum S, look for S - K.\",\"expected_complexity\":\"Time: O(N), Space: O(N)\",\"ideal_answer\":\"\",\"scenario\":\"\",\"correct_option\":\"\",\"explanation\":\"\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.316Z\"},\"test_cases\":[{\"id\":17,\"question_id\":9,\"input\":\"3\\n1 1 1\\n2\",\"expected_output\":\"2\",\"is_hidden\":false,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.322Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.322Z\"},{\"id\":18,\"question_id\":9,\"input\":\"3\\n1 -1 0\\n0\",\"expected_output\":\"3\",\"is_hidden\":true,\"explanation\":\"\",\"order_index\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.328Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T07:52:40.328Z\"}],\"hints\":[{\"id\":17,\"question_id\":9,\"type\":\"hint\",\"content\":\"Think about prefix sums and what previous sum would be needed to produce K.\",\"order_index\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-