INSERT INTO `interview_question_details` VALUES (1,1,'2 <= N <= 10^5\n-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9\nExactly one valid answer exists.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Traverse the array once and use a HashMap to store previously visited numbers and their indices. For each number, check whether target - nums[i] already exists.','Time: O(N), Space: O(N)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:39.716','2026-09-17 07:52:39.716'),(2,2,'1 <= s.length, t.length <= 10^5\nStrings contain lowercase English letters.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Count the frequency of every character in the first string and compare it with the frequency of characters in the second string using a HashMap or frequency array.','Time: O(N), Space: O(K)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:39.820','2026-09-17 07:52:39.820'),(3,3,'1 <= s.length <= 10^5\ns consists of lowercase English letters.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Build a frequency map for all characters, then make a second pass through the string and return the index of the first character whose frequency is one.','Time: O(N), Space: O(K)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:39.900','2026-09-17 07:52:39.900'),(4,4,'1 <= N <= 10^4\n1 <= word.length <= 100\nWords contain lowercase English letters.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Create a character-frequency signature for each word and use that signature as a HashMap key. Words with the same signature belong to the same group.','Time: O(N * L), Space: O(N * L)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:39.983','2026-09-17 07:52:39.983'),(5,5,'0 <= s.length <= 10^5\ns consists of printable ASCII characters.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Use a sliding window with two pointers and a HashMap storing the most recent index of each character.','Time: O(N), Space: O(K)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.058','2026-09-17 07:52:40.058'),(6,6,'1 <= N <= 10^5\n-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9\nA majority element always exists.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Use the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm to maintain a candidate and a count while traversing the array.','Time: O(N), Space: O(1)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.131','2026-09-17 07:52:40.131'),(7,7,'0 <= N <= 10^5\n-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9\nDuplicate values may exist.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Insert all values into a HashSet. Start counting a sequence only when the current value has no predecessor, then repeatedly check for the next consecutive value.','Time: O(N) average, Space: O(N)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.200','2026-09-17 07:52:40.200'),(8,8,'2 <= N <= 10^5\n-30 <= nums[i] <= 30\nThe result fits within a 32-bit signed integer.\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Calculate prefix products from left to right and suffix products from right to left without using division.','Time: O(N), Space: O(1) auxiliary excluding the output array','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.261','2026-09-17 07:52:40.261'),(9,9,'1 <= N <= 10^5\n-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\n-10^9 <= K <= 10^9\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Maintain a running prefix sum and use a HashMap to store the frequency of previous prefix sums. For the current sum S, look for S - K.','Time: O(N), Space: O(N)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.316','2026-09-17 07:52:40.316'),(10,10,'1 <= s.length <= 10^5\ns contains only (, ), {, }, [, ].\nTime Limit: 2.0s\nMemory Limit: 256MB','Use a stack to store opening brackets and verify that every closing bracket matches the most recently opened bracket.','Time: O(N), Space: O(N)','','','','','2026-09-17 07:52:40.382','2026-09-17 07:52:40.382'),(11,11,'','','','','500M new URLs per month and 50B redirects per month. Read/write ratio is approximately 100:1. Redirect latency should be below 10ms with 99.99% availability.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.376','2026-09-17 07:55:23.376'),(12,12,'','','','','10M daily active users with up to 1M concurrent connections. Messages should normally be delivered within 500ms. The system must support message persistence and temporary offline users.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.432','2026-09-17 07:55:23.432'),(13,13,'','','','','5M daily active users and 500K video uploads per day. Popular videos may receive millions of views. The system should support adaptive streaming and high availability.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.480','2026-09-17 07:55:23.480'),(14,14,'','','','','2M daily users, 100K concurrent users during peak hours, and 200K orders per day. Order creation and payment operations require strong consistency while restaurant discovery can tolerate eventual consistency.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.532','2026-09-17 07:55:23.532'),(15,15,'','','','','5M daily active users and 500K concurrent drivers. Location updates can arrive every few seconds. Ride matching should normally complete within 2 seconds.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.635','2026-09-17 07:55:23.635'),(16,16,'','','','','The platform receives 1M requests per second across multiple regions. Different APIs may have different limits per user, IP address, or API key. Rate-limit decisions should normally complete within 5ms.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.732','2026-09-17 07:55:23.732'),(17,17,'','','','','100M notifications per day with large traffic bursts. Notifications should be processed asynchronously, retried when providers fail, and should not block the application\'s main request path.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.814','2026-09-17 07:55:23.814'),(18,18,'','','','','50M users with 10PB of stored data. Individual files can range from a few KB to several GB. The system must provide durable storage and efficient downloads.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.882','2026-09-17 07:55:23.882'),(19,19,'','','','','10M daily users with 100K concurrent users during major sales. Product browsing is read-heavy, while inventory and order operations require strong consistency.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.946','2026-09-17 07:55:23.946'),(20,20,'','','','','100 active collaborators per document with typing latency below 50ms. The system must support document revisions, concurrent edits, and users reconnecting after temporary network failures.','','','2026-09-17 07:55:23.998','2026-09-17 07:55:23.998'),(21,21,'Employees without a valid department should not appear. Handle salary ties appropriately.','Use JOIN between employees and departments, then use ROW_NUMBER() or DENSE_RANK() with PARTITION BY department_id to identify the highest-paid employees in each department.','','','Tables required: employees, departments. Employees belong to departments and have salary information. Return the top 3 employees per department.','','','2026-09-17 07:59:35.694','2026-09-17 07:59:35.694'),(22,22,'Customers with only pending or refunded orders should also be included.','Use LEFT JOIN with the date and status conditions applied correctly, then identify customers whose matching order is NULL.','','','Tables required: customers and orders. A customer can have multiple orders. Only completed orders should be considered.','','','2026-09-17 07:59:35.730','2026-09-17 07:59:35.730'),(23,23,'Products with no completed sales should not be considered. Handle multiple products having the same total quantity.','Join products with categories and order_items, filter completed orders, aggregate quantity by product, and use a window function to rank products within each category.','','','Tables required: products, categories, order_items, and orders. Only completed orders should contribute to sales calculations.','','','2026-09-17 07:59:35.774','2026-09-17 07:59:35.774'),(24,24,'Return employee name, department name, salary, and department average salary.','Calculate the department-level average salary using a subquery or window function, then compare each employee\'s salary against the corresponding department average.','','','Tables required: employees and departments. Each employee belongs to a department and has a salary.','','','2026-09-17 07:59:35.821','2026-09-17 07:59:35.821'),(25,25,'A customer must have purchased at least 3 distinct products and products from at least 2 distinct categories.','Join all related tables, filter completed orders, group by customer, calculate COUNT(DISTINCT product_id), COUNT(DISTINCT category_id), and SUM of item quantity multiplied by product price.','','','Tables required: customers, orders, order_items, products, and categories. Only completed orders should be included.','','','2026-09-17 07:59:35.873','2026-09-17 07:59:35.873'),(26,26,'Use React and map() to render the products.','','','','Display the given products as simple cards. Each card should show the product name and price.','','','2026-09-17 08:01:12.095','2026-09-17 08:01:12.095'),(27,27,'Use React useState for the counter value.','','','','The counter starts at 0. Clicking + increases the value by 1 and clicking - decreases it by 1.','','','2026-09-17 08:01:12.133','2026-09-17 08:01:12.133'),(28,28,'Filtering should work without reloading the page.','','','','Display the users in a list. When the user types in the search box, show only matching names.','','','2026-09-17 08:01:12.195','2026-09-17 08:01:12.195'),(29,29,'Use useState to store the todo items.','','','','Provide an input and Add button. When the button is clicked, add the entered task to the todo list.','','','2026-09-17 08:01:12.248','2026-09-17 08:01:12.248'),(30,30,'Use React state to control the input type.','','','','Initially show the password as hidden. Clicking the button should switch between password and text input types.','','','2026-09-17 08:01:12.295','2026-09-17 08:01:12.295'),(31,31,'User name must not be empty. Return HTTP 400 for an empty name and HTTP 201 when a user is created.','Store users in memory and handle POST /users.','','','','','','2026-09-17 08:02:22.678','2026-09-17 08:02:22.678'),(32,32,'Return HTTP 200 when the user exists and HTTP 404 when the user does not exist.','Find the user by ID from an in-memory list.','','','','','','2026-09-17 08:02:22.725','2026-09-17 08:02:22.725'),(33,33,'GET /products should return all products. A category query parameter should return only matching products.','Read the category query parameter and filter the products when it is provided.','','','','','','2026-09-17 08:02:22.761','2026-09-17 08:02:22.761'),(34,34,'Use PATCH /users/:id. Return HTTP 200 after a successful update and HTTP 404 when the user does not exist.','Find the user by ID and update the name using the request body.','','','','','','2026-09-17 08:02:22.804','2026-09-17 08:02:22.804'),(35,35,'Use DELETE /tasks/:id. Return HTTP 200 when the task is deleted and HTTP 404 when the task does not exist.','Find the task by ID and remove it from the list.','','','','','','2026-09-17 08:02:22.844','2026-09-17 08:02:22.844'),(36,36,'','','','','','A','Linux is an operating system used to manage computer hardware and software resources.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.252','2026-09-17 08:27:36.252'),(37,37,'','','','','','B','A process is a program that is currently being executed.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.292','2026-09-17 08:27:36.292'),(38,38,'','','','','','C','A thread is the smallest unit of execution within a process.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.330','2026-09-17 08:27:36.330'),(39,39,'','','','','','A','RAM is volatile memory, so its contents are lost when power is turned off.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.368','2026-09-17 08:27:36.368'),(40,40,'','','','','','D','The CPU executes instructions and performs calculations required by programs.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.408','2026-09-17 08:27:36.408'),(41,41,'','','','','','B','A stack follows Last In, First Out (LIFO).','2026-09-17 08:27:36.451','2026-09-17 08:27:36.451'),(42,42,'','','','','','A','A queue follows First In, First Out (FIFO).','2026-09-17 08:27:36.485','2026-09-17 08:27:36.485'),(43,43,'','','','','','C','Binary search eliminates half of the remaining elements at each step, giving O(log N) time.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.519','2026-09-17 08:27:36.519'),(44,44,'','','','','','A','Arrays provide direct access using an index, which takes O(1) time.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.551','2026-09-17 08:27:36.551'),(45,45,'','','','','','D','A linked list consists of nodes where each node stores data and a reference to another node.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.585','2026-09-17 08:27:36.585'),(46,46,'','','','','','B','With a good hash function and low collision rate, hash table lookup is O(1) on average.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.618','2026-09-17 08:27:36.618'),(47,47,'','','','','','C','Each node in a binary tree can have at most two children.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.656','2026-09-17 08:27:36.656'),(48,48,'','','','','','A','BFS uses a queue to process nodes level by level.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.689','2026-09-17 08:27:36.689'),(49,49,'','','','','','D','Iterative DFS commonly uses a stack. Recursive DFS uses the call stack.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.718','2026-09-17 08:27:36.718'),(50,50,'','','','','','B','SQL is used to create, read, update, and delete data in relational databases.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.754','2026-09-17 08:27:36.754'),(51,51,'','','','','','C','A primary key uniquely identifies each row in a table.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.776','2026-09-17 08:27:36.776'),(52,52,'','','','','','A','A foreign key creates a relationship between tables by referencing a key in another table.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.806','2026-09-17 08:27:36.806'),(53,53,'','','','','','D','Normalization reduces unnecessary data duplication and helps maintain data consistency.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.838','2026-09-17 08:27:36.838'),(54,54,'','','','','','B','GET is commonly used to request and retrieve data from a server.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.872','2026-09-17 08:27:36.872'),(55,55,'','','','','','A','POST is commonly used to submit data and create a new resource.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.901','2026-09-17 08:27:36.901'),(56,56,'','','','','','C','404 means that the requested resource could not be found.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.924','2026-09-17 08:27:36.924'),(57,57,'','','','','','D','500 indicates an internal server error.','2026-09-17 08:27:36.958','2026-09-17 08:27:36.958'),(58,58,'','','','','','A','TCP provides reliable, ordered, connection-oriented data transmission.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.001','2026-09-17 08:27:37.001'),(59,59,'','','','','','C','UDP is connectionless and does not provide TCP-style guarantees of delivery and ordering.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.036','2026-09-17 08:27:37.036'),(60,60,'','','','','','B','DNS translates domain names such as example.com into IP addresses.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.090','2026-09-17 08:27:37.090'),(61,61,'','','','','','A','Encapsulation bundles data and related methods together and can restrict direct access to internal state.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.125','2026-09-17 08:27:37.125'),(62,62,'','','','','','D','Inheritance allows a class to reuse or extend the properties and methods of another class.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.180','2026-09-17 08:27:37.180'),(63,63,'','','','','','C','Polymorphism allows the same interface or method call to have different behavior depending on the object.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.220','2026-09-17 08:27:37.220'),(64,64,'','','','','','B','A compiler translates source code into another form, commonly machine code or an intermediate representation.','2026-09-17 08:27:37.273','2026-09-17 08:27:37.273'),(65,65,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - describe the disagreement briefly. Task - explain your responsibility in resolving it. Action - describe how you listened, communicated calmly, and worked toward a solution. Result - explain how the conflict was resolved and what you learned.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.670','2026-09-17 08:30:41.670'),(66,66,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - describe the task or activity. Task - explain why leadership was needed. Action - explain how you organized the team, assigned responsibilities, and kept everyone involved. Result - describe the outcome and what you learned about leadership.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.718','2026-09-17 08:30:41.718'),(67,67,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - explain the task and what went wrong. Task - describe your responsibility. Action - explain how you accepted the mistake, identified the cause, and took corrective action. Result - describe the outcome and the lesson learned.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.751','2026-09-17 08:30:41.751'),(68,68,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - describe the pressure or deadline. Task - explain what needed to be completed. Action - describe how you prioritized work, managed your time, and stayed focused. Result - explain whether you completed the task and what you learned.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.776','2026-09-17 08:30:41.776'),(69,69,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - explain why the teammate was struggling. Task - describe your role or responsibility. Action - explain how you understood their problem and provided guidance or support. Result - describe how the teammate or team benefited.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.817','2026-09-17 08:30:41.817'),(70,70,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - explain the difficult situation. Task - describe the decision you were responsible for. Action - explain how you considered the available options, risks, and consequences. Result - describe the outcome and what you learned.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.855','2026-09-17 08:30:41.855'),(71,71,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - describe when you received the feedback. Task - explain what you were responsible for. Action - describe how you listened, understood the feedback, and made improvements. Result - explain how your performance changed afterward.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.888','2026-09-17 08:30:41.888'),(72,72,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - explain the original plan and what changed. Task - describe what you still needed to accomplish. Action - explain how you adjusted your approach and communicated the changes. Result - describe the final outcome.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.917','2026-09-17 08:30:41.917'),(73,73,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - describe why the team was losing motivation. Task - explain your responsibility. Action - describe how you encouraged the team, clarified goals, divided work, or supported teammates. Result - explain how the team\'s motivation and progress improved.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.951','2026-09-17 08:30:41.951'),(74,74,'','','','Use the STAR format: Situation - explain the team project and the problem. Task - describe your responsibility. Action - explain how you acknowledged the issue, communicated with the team, and worked on a solution. Result - describe the final outcome and what you learned about accountability.','','','','2026-09-17 08:30:41.972','2026-09-17 08:30:41.972');
